---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../site.config';
import { t } from '../i18n/en';

const strings = t();
const updated = '2026-11-05';
const email = siteConfig.contactEmail;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={strings.privacyStubTitle}
  description={`Privacy policy for ${siteConfig.name} — what the stand brief collects and how it is shared with Brijnco.`}
  path="/privacy"
>
  <article class="container section prose">
    <h1>{strings.privacyStubTitle}</h1>
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--rule">{strings.lastUpdated}: {updated}</p>

    <div class="stack" style="gap: 0.25rem;">
      <p>
        This notice explains how {siteConfig.name} ({siteConfig.domain.replace('https://', '')}) handles
        personal information. It is written to align with the Australian Privacy Principles; have it
        reviewed before running paid campaigns at scale.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {siteConfig.name} is an independent calendar of Australian trade shows, operated in connection
        with <strong>{siteConfig.author}</strong>, an Australian exhibition stand builder. We are not a
        show organiser and are not affiliated with the shows or venues listed.
        See <a href="/about">how dates are checked, and how this site relates to {siteConfig.author}</a>.
        {email && (
          <>
            {' '}Contact: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
          </>
        )}
      </p>

      <h2>What the stand brief collects</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit a stand brief we collect what you enter — name, work email, phone, company,
        website, target show, stand size and type, budget band, timeline, design-asset status, your
        message and how you heard about us — plus the page address, any campaign (UTM) tags, and the
        date and time of submission. For security and spam prevention our endpoint also sees your IP
        address, approximate country and browser type.
      </p>

      <h2>How it is used and shared</h2>
      <p>
        Your brief is sent to <strong>{siteConfig.author}</strong> so they can contact you about
        exhibition stand services — that is the purpose of the form. We assign a simple priority
        (hot / warm / cold) from your budget, timeline, stand size and show date to help them respond.
        We do not sell your information.
      </p>
      <p>Service providers that process the brief on our behalf:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — website hosting and the serverless form endpoint.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivers the brief by email to {siteConfig.author}’s inbox.</li>
        <li>
          Optionally, a workflow or CRM tool connected by webhook to log enquiries. Some providers may
          store data outside Australia.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        The website itself does not keep a database of briefs. Copies are held in {siteConfig.author}’s
        email and any connected CRM for as long as needed to respond and manage the business
        relationship, then deleted or de-identified.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics &amp; cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics 4, with IP anonymisation, to see which pages are useful. GA4 sets
        first-party cookies. Details are in the <a href="/cookies">Cookie policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to access or correct the personal information we hold about you, or ask us to delete
        it{email ? (
          <>
            {' '}— email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
          </>
        ) : ''}. If you are unhappy with how we handled your information you can contact the Office of
        the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC).
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
